  "question": {
    "text": "If $\\operatorname{Lim}_{x \\rightarrow 0}\\left(\\frac{\\tan x}{x}\\right)^{\\frac{1}{x^2}}=p$, then $96 \\log _e p$ is equal to ______"
  },
  "options": [],
  "correct_answer": "32",
  "solution": {
    "text": "$P=\\lim _{x \\rightarrow 0}\\left(\\frac{\\tan x}{x}\\right)^{\\frac{1}{x^2}}$<br/>$\\Rightarrow \\mathrm{P}=\\mathrm{e}^{\\lim _{\\mathrm{x} \\rightarrow 0}\\left(\\frac{\\tan x-\\mathrm{x}}{\\mathrm{x}^3}\\right)}$<br/>$=\\mathrm{e}^{\\lim _{x \\rightarrow 0} \\frac{\\left(x+\\frac{x^3}{3}+\\frac{2 x^5}{15}+\\ldots . .-x\\right)}{x^3}}$<br/>$=e^{1 / 3}$<br/>$\\therefore 96 \\log _{\\mathrm{e}}^{\\mathrm{p}}=96 \\times \\frac{1}{3}=32$"
  }
}